{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded","id":906006,"title":"[2E] On the numbers of Dragon Blooded","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-02T15:32:26-07:00","id":906006,"title":"[2E] On the numbers of Dragon Blooded","content":"I used the 2E tag because we don't have much (I think) to go on on DB population dynamics yet. Anyhow - I was talking to my group (5 players) about running a generational DB game in the <b>300's </b>when the new 3E book comes out. One player proposed the group be a children of two married outcaste DB's forming a Minor Household, and how the PC's try to make the house larger and possibly into a great house over time. Loads of other ideas great ideas too, and lots of room for great stories for me to tell, we all agree to play.<br /> <br /> The reason I'm writing though - is that a couple of my players said they'd play male PC's who assemble a large harem of women and summoned elementals whom they get pregnant, and just through sheer numbers have a massive number of DB Exalted children. I've always been a bit skeptical of this idea actually working out in the world of Exalted.<br /> <br /> (1) The expense alone could be ruinous.<br /> (2) The (2e) Canon is that DB's in the Dynasty don't really have that many children, the average being <b>8 per century</b> (for dual exalted couples) It does acknowledge that some DB couples have lots of children, but that is the exception and not the norm<br /> (3) A Minor House pumping out dozens of DB children a year will eventually get noticed by the Great Houses.<br /> (4) Such notice will in fact, be lethal. Great Houses don't like competition, and any minor house having even dozens of Children a year will be curb stomped into the ground without the protection of a Great House.<br /> (5) The Empress herself would likely not tolerate a Minor House upending her balance and control by having say,<b> 2500 new Exalted in a century</b>.<br /> (6) Even it were allowed, a house expanding so fast would lose cohesion and central control would be impossible. Other houses would poach DB's in marriages, and the time and attention required to build relationships with the parent(s) to have a bond to their house wouldn't be possible with too many children.<br /> <br /> Counterpoints<br /> (1) The Empire always needs Dynasts and Dragonbloods to do many of the jobs - some 1e books I believe and maybe 2e books imply there are not enough DBs to go around for all of the work needed.<br /> (2) Assassinations simply over a house having &quot;too many&quot; DB's might compromise the empire and reduce fertility rates to unsustainable levels.<br /> <br /> Is this line of thinking reasonable/unreasonable? What am I missing? Further thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":".  Reason: Because I forgot some words. :P 06-02-2016, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T15:37:46-07:00","id":906008,"title":"","content":"Exaltation is a blessing of the Dragons, not an exact science. Those who try to take advantage of the Dragon's munificence will surely face a high karmic debt.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* In other words, your player is probably only going to have a small number of children actually Exalt, such that the entire project is seen as a complete joke by the rest of the Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 06-02-2016, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T15:44:08-07:00","id":906013,"title":"","content":"The 2e books have terrible, nonsense population dynamics; to make any sense of the numbers at all, you end up in houserule country. One of the following things needs to be true:<br /> <br /> 1) Mortality among the Dragon-Blooded is staggeringly high, on the order of constant Black Plague-level population depletion.<br /> 2) Exaltation rate is very, very low even among direct children of Dragon-Blooded - say, 1/10 or 1/100, before breeding gets involved. If one of the parents is mortal, these numbers drop off sharply.<br /> <br /> (I favor #2.)<br /> <br /> I would recommend ignoring anything the book says about summoned elementals shifting these numbers around, because it creates precisely the sort of weird &quot;Why has no one...?&quot; problems you're describing. Your best odds of having Exalted children should come of DB/DB pairings; anything else is a shot in the dark. This has the added benefit of removing the incentives for a lot of behavior that I'd rather not deal with in-game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 06-02-2016, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T15:47:53-07:00","id":906018,"title":"","content":"This topic... it's so late...<br /> <br /> \u200bJust... just tell your players to make characters who treat women with respect. Don't play Immortan Joe.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T15:57:31-07:00","id":906028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=906013#post906013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 2e books have terrible, nonsense population dynamics; to make any sense of the numbers at all, you end up in houserule country. One of the following things needs to be true:<br /> <br /> 1) Mortality among the Dragon-Blooded is staggeringly high, on the order of constant Black Plague-level population depletion.<br /> 2) Exaltation rate is very, very low even among direct children of Dragon-Blooded - say, 1/10 or 1/100, before breeding gets involved. If one of the parents is mortal, these numbers drop off sharply.<br /> <br /> (I favor #2.)<br /> <br /> I would recommend ignoring anything the book says about summoned elementals shifting these numbers around, because it creates precisely the sort of weird &quot;Why has no one...?&quot; problems you're describing. Your best odds of having Exalted children should come of DB/DB pairings; anything else is a shot in the dark. This has the added benefit of removing the incentives for a lot of behavior that I'd rather not deal with in-game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like your thinking. #1 would not only imply that Dragon Blood die in battle a lot, but also meet an amazing number of &quot;accidents&quot; which would imply an unhealthy level of intrigue. I think it would go deeply into the &quot;unfun&quot; territory for my games. #2 makes much more sense to have just 10,000 DBs. The other idea is #3, there are way more than 10,000 DBs in the realm alone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=906018#post906018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This topic... it's so late...</div> </div> </div> </div>Late topic...? I haven't posted here much in years, so... sorry?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=906018#post906018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bJust... just tell your players to make characters who treat women with respect. Don't play Immortan Joe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon Bloods canonically don't have to treat mortal slaves with any respect at all. To be real though: Those two male players who are simply thinking through a problem &quot;logically&quot; and not using any emotional computing power to understand how the logistics alone of a massive family and the administration structure it require would defeat such an endeavor. They're also younger and single, not married with 5 kids like I am. I'm not too worried. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":". 06-02-2016, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T16:03:06-07:00","id":906031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=906028#post906028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like your thinking. #1 would not only imply that Dragon Blood die in battle a lot, but also meet an amazing number of &quot;accidents&quot; which would imply an unhealthy level of intrigue. I think it would go deeply into the &quot;unfun&quot; territory for my games. #2 makes much more sense to have just 10,000 DBs. The other idea is #3, there are way more than 10,000 DBs in the realm alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the other possibility, yeah - if the number of Dragon-Blooded is growing, you can stretch things some. Though only <i>some</i> - even a very slight growth rate gives you huge numbers over 700+ years.<br /> <br /> #1 seems like it would warp the Realm in some pretty unfun ways, yeah. &quot;Hey, I went back for my ten-year high school reunion! Half of us are dead.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T16:17:46-07:00","id":906040,"title":"","content":"If you want to let them see why these things don't work out, consider having the elemental and mortal breeding thin the blood so fast that the children or grandchildren have no exalted offspring then consider that it takes at least a decade and possibly two before you start to see results. In that time you will have a lot of children being raised in an environment not at all conducive to making them loyal. You can't have them kill each other in some sort of gladiatorial survival of the fittest because that doesn't improve the chances of Exaltation at all. The remaining elemental blooded children are probably going to want a role more important than &quot;servant to the sibling who actually managed to Exalt&quot;. The ones who do exalt are probably going to hate each other almost as much as they hate their sires, and Sol only knows how many of them are going to get a different Exaltation and try to blow the whole thing up.<br /> <br /> Also, treat the Wyld Revocation power like unerrated Zeal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T16:44:52-07:00","id":906052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=906031#post906031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the other possibility, yeah - if the number of Dragon-Blooded is growing, you can stretch things some. Though only <i>some</i> - even a very slight growth rate gives you huge numbers over 700+ years.<br /> <br /> #1 seems like it would warp the Realm in some pretty unfun ways, yeah. &quot;Hey, I went back for my ten-year high school reunion! Half of us are dead.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact, you have a great point for #3 actually, given that I'll set the game in the 300's. Simply say there are 10,000 DBs now in 302 or whatever, as the canon reproduction rates don't have to make sense for 768, as I'm not starting then.<br /> <br /> We know, canonically that the number of DB's was deeply depleted after the Contagion. Using my half remembered 1e and 2e canon, there were about 1 to 3 million DBs. 90% die in the great contagion. Now down 100k - 300k DBs. Then the absolutely massive fair folk attack happens. Given how dire the canon is, say 97.5% die. We're now down to 2500 to 7500. The Empress has to use the Realm defence grid again to kill the Seven tigers and their armies, and was loathe to do so given the size of the armies involved.<br /> <br /> Lets say this reduces the numbers even further, by half, as we know before 100 in 2e canon - the empress enough troops for three failed and costly invasions of the Scavanger lands. 1250 to 3750 - and spread all over creation. Take the average, 2500, Yikes. Even 50 years later by my calculations using simply the standard DB reproduction rate, gives 18,643 DB by the year 57. Yeeah.... I sincerely hope the 3E designers have a much tighter grasp of DB reproduction rates mathematically, or have good assumptions for a higher death rate, or a lower DB exaltation rate or something.<br /> <br /> That or there had to be truly few DBs surviving, more like 1000 or less, according to the setting canon. Food for thought.<br /> <br /> Edit: My spreadsheet is at work - but 18,643 is an over estimate. 2500 DBs do not have hermaphroditic reproduction rates and I need to check again the assumption for 1250 breeding females. Also - exaltation rate. I'm assuming one. Heck this might actually be manageable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":".  Calculations too high 06-03-2016, 01:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T16:54:51-07:00","id":906056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=906028#post906028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Late topic...? I haven't posted here much in years, so... sorry?</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bNo no, let me explain.<br /> <br /> This subject comes up a lot. It's one that particularly distresses me, and I often expend a lot of energy on arguing against it.<br /> <br /> It is also late at night for me at this time.<br /> <br /> As it is, your talk of the impractical logistics of it all is on the right track, so stay the course! Do it for your poor oul Levi.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T17:41:55-07:00","id":906076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=906028#post906028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon Bloods canonically don't have to treat mortal slaves with any respect at all. To be real though: Those two male players who are simply thinking through a problem &quot;logically&quot; and not using any emotional computing power to understand how the logistics alone of a massive family and the administration structure it require would defeat such an endeavor. They're also younger and single, not married with 5 kids like I am. I'm not too worried. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Try to keep in mind that Dynasts are not only set apart by their magical birthright but also their <i>social</i> birthright. They are members of an exclusive ruling caste which is subject to its own rules of honour and conduct.<br /> <br /> To me the idea that a Dynastic House should breed as many bastard Dragon-Bloods as possible is scarcely more credible than, say, a clan from Legend of Five Rings breeding as many samurai as possible, or the Targaryens of SoIAF breeding as many white-haired children as possible. It's just not the way their society works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 06-02-2016, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T17:44:53-07:00","id":906079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=906056#post906056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bNo no, let me explain.<br /> <br /> This subject comes up a lot. It's one that particularly distresses me, and I often expend a lot of energy on arguing against it.<br /> <br /> It is also late at night for me at this time.<br /> <br /> As it is, your talk of the impractical logistics of it all is on the right track, so stay the course! Do it for your poor oul Levi.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thanks for the explanation. Given the mathematical borkedness of DB fertility in 2E - I'm not surprised this is a relatively common topic for you to come across.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T19:04:31-07:00","id":906121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=906013#post906013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2) Exaltation rate is very, very low even among direct children of Dragon-Blooded - say, 1/10 or 1/100, before breeding gets involved. If one of the parents is mortal, these numbers drop off sharply.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'll just mention that, in 1st ed, the rules for seeing if the child of a DB and mortal exalted was &quot;roll a dice, they exalt on a 10&quot;. So, a 1/10 exaltation rate is pretty reasonable.<br /> <br /> I'd also mention that &quot;8 per century&quot; is probably something they only do in the first century, after that they probably stop, especially if they have a DB kid or two.<br /> <br /> I mean, my parents could have had more kids 10 years after me and my sister, but they didn't want to. They already had enough, why have more? And that's pretty common for most families.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, to the OP: I think you're on track with how impractical it is. Every Realm family could do this, but they don't: clearly, the social order does not approve. Immaculates will say you're being immoral and not treating the Exaltation with the respect the Dragons require, and the other families (and Empress!) will fear your rising power.<br /> <br /> Also... it's going to take 10-20 years before the kids exalt, and during that time you're going to have to raise a ton of kids, the daughters and sons of slaves, so you can't give each much attention. And it'll definitely stretch your money.<br /> It wouldn't shock me if in 20 years a group of DB kids decide to overthrow their father for the way he treated them and their mothers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T20:38:23-07:00","id":906162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=906121#post906121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll just mention that, in 1st ed, the rules for seeing if the child of a DB and mortal exalted was &quot;roll a dice, they exalt on a 10&quot;. So, a 1/10 exaltation rate is pretty reasonable.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was pre-modifiers, though; if the parents were Dragon-Blooded, it got up to something like 40-50%, which is <i>hilariously</i> too many kids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T20:41:14-07:00","id":906165,"title":"","content":"Was it? I thought it was 1/10 per DB parent, with a +1 for a Breeding 4 parent, and +2 for a Breeding 5 parent.<br /> So, two Breeding 5 parents would have a 60% chance per kid, but two Breeding 1 parents would only have a 20% chance.<br /> <br /> I don't actually have the 1st ed DB book, this is going from memory, so I might be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T22:24:39-07:00","id":906215,"title":"","content":"I've reread the 1E and 2E DB books this evening about DB culture and have more thoughts on this. I agree with the thought that that there is social stigma against having too many children is simply of a fact of a, by definition, DB's are an exclusive ruling caste. It's not an exclusive club if everyone gets to join it. There is a social contract of being a DB, as mentioned earlier.<br /> <br /> In both 1E and 2E canon it mentions that the Empress keeps the DB's away from the regular population and insulates them with the patricians. The DB's are considered form of Gods Amongst Men. 250 DB's a year in a population canonically of 10,000 in one house hold (2.5% growth) - if copied - would be an unmanageable increase and violate the long term security of the Empire for the Scarlet Empress. In fact, I think, once considering the financial costs alone - there are a multitude of subtle disincentives for trying to have a large family too quickly. 2e DB Manual of Power mentions:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The amount of jade a Dynast actually receives from her family is determined by a ludicrously complex formula that takes many factors into consideration. Those factors include age, education, marital status, whether one\u2019s spouse is mortal or Dragon-Blooded, service to the family, service to the legions, service to the Wyld Hunt, service to the Empress, number of children produced, number of children Exalted and the rarity and strategic importance of any particular skills the Dragon-Blood possesses. </div> </div> </div>A slow, manageable increase in DB population numbers is probably a good thing for the empire as a whole - it is culturally manageable. If a male DB wants to marry a patrician/dynastic mortal, live in a manse with the correct element and a Dragon's Nest power (base bonus 3+1+2 before breeding)/10 = 60% per child, have one kid a year - and can afford it - would at least be seen as <i>playing by the rules.</i> He would have to make a significant effort into making enough money to pay resources 3 or 4 a year, per child, for tutoring and primary school. Each child that exalts requires a resources 4 or 5 for placement in a secondary school. He likely didn't start out with that manse, and would have to have built it himself, or traded favors etc to get it.<br /> <br /> The amount of economic activity he would have to generate per year would likely be multiple Resource 5's and likely be of great benefit to his House and the Empire's economy as a whole. He would also make enemies, and likely be a target simply because his business holdings are so large that an ambitious or capricious DB might want to eat a piece of his pie. It would take a lot of hard work to manage correctly and successfully. Other DB's would likely be proud of him at some level for managing to pull it off even if they thought poorly of his blood.<br /> <br /> i.e.<br /> &quot;He obviously likes to rut a lot with those mortal wive's of his, and produces DB's of poor blood, but by the Dragon's, 60 exalted children in a hundred years - and he manages three separate business holdings to pay for it all! I doubt that the man has slept more than 4 hours a day for over a century! I bet he expends most of essence just trying to stay awake!&quot; (laughter ensues) This is assuming he somehow manages to continuously have a legitimate mortal child per year.<br /> <br /> A higher breeding male DB (4 to 6) likely would be of a higher social class and expected to marry a female DB, and it would be exceptional, and likely scandalous circumstances where they marry a mortal.<br /> <br /> I think Lookshy is much the same as the realm in this regard. While they talk about, and give lip service to having more children - really, too many too fast would undermine the cohesive military structure and society. Look at the baby boomers IRL- one of the reasons for the mass cultural rebellion of the 60s and 70s was there were simply too many kids for the adults to control. (Or so my boomer parents tell me.)<br /> <br /> Likely - Outcaste DB's in the threshold have tried this, but can't educate the children well enough, as well - suffer from a much, much higher death rate. If one squints a bit - I think there are arguably setting reasons of the DB population being what it is. Likely, 10,000 DB's or there abouts, is what the Empress and the Sidereals can control with only somewhat frequent peasant rebellions and attempts at regicidal civil war. Canon 2e mentions that the major failing of the Shogunate was near constant civil war and frequent civil strife.<br /> <br /> I think the original writers of 1e and 2e DB books did goof on not calculating through what their numbers actually implied. I think if one alters their head canon just a titch - you can use DB breeding rates in a 1e or 2e game as is, and it makes sense. PC's of course, can upend that goofing around. I'm very, very curious to see what the Dev's pull out of their hat for DB breeding rates, or setting changes, or simply a better explanation (like mine - 10,000 is what the Empress can control) or some combination of all of the above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":".  Spelling 06-03-2016, 01:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T23:23:33-07:00","id":906243,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I basically see every part of the setting's statements on the Realm DB population as totally bonkers.<br /> <br /> The Empress doesn't want too many DBs for her to control... so she creates a system which incentivizes them to keep as many of such children a secret (and so, outside of her influence) as possible. The Great Houses want to keep their Breeding strong... so they take a bunch of elaborate measures, which end up giving a lower DB birth rate per capita than the far lower-Breeding Lookshy. Most Dynasts never Exalt... which is why you almost never see or hear about unExalted Dynasts, and when you do, they're treated as these terrible pariahs for doing what the majority of people do. Dynasts are infamously hedonistic, with prostitutes and orgies (as well as Neomah, who can magically increase the odds of making DB babies) mentioned constantly... so they practice stellar birth control at all times. Yes, even reckless males on assignments overseas.<br /> <br /> It's bizarre. My advice: ignore everything.<br /> <br /> Well, to be more exact, ignore everything you dislike. The version presented by the game is totally incoherent, so there's no great loss if you throw the nursery out with the swimming pool. Cut anything and everything which doesn't seem cool for the game you want to run, and make things up to cover. My personal headcanon is that DBs have (but may not have had, before the Great Contagion) a low fertility rate amongst themselves, and a VERY low rate with non-DBs. Their children do usually exalt, though - especially if both parents are DBs, and if they have high Essence. This means:<ul><li>Ambitious Dynasts cannot churn out supersoldier armies in secret, because makin' babies that fast is practically impossible.</li> <li>DB-DB couplings really are the best way to keep your bloodline going.</li> <li>UnExalted Dynasts are rare, and a huge blow to their parents.</li> <li>DBs married to mortals have suffered a crippling loss of status, or other extreme fate, rather than this happening constantly due to force of numbers.</li> <li>Most DBs in The Realm had two (and failing that, one) Dragon-Blooded parent, rather than most being born to two unExalted Dynasts (again by force of numbers).</li> </ul><br /> In other words, it clears up my main objections. But other objections, requiring other solutions, are perfectly reasonable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T23:45:27-07:00","id":906256,"title":"","content":"Actually, non-Exalted dynasts are mentioned a fair bit, but not a ton, because, well, they're not very interesting.<br /> <br /> But I agree with your general point, that it's not consistent and wasn't very well thought through.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T01:35:01-07:00","id":906281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=906018#post906018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This topic... it's so late...<br /> <br /> \u200bJust... just tell your players to make characters who treat women with respect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah you probably should just-<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=906018#post906018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't play Immortan Joe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoa whoa Levi, let's not get crazy here. Everyone should feel free lead their army of war-boys to die historic on the Fury Road.<br /> <br /> <br /> More seriously, since we don't really know how DB exaltation in third edition works, I'd probably say that any attempt to just squeeze out a ton of DBs has the Dragons go &quot;Fuck you, you don't respect the power of your blood, you don't get any more.&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's not a matter of genetics or science, it's a divine fire that kindles in the blood of a few. There is something to be gained by saying that it really isn't, and every DB exaltation is just a matter of pure breeding, but I think it would lose something if that were true. You have a blessed lineage, a line of heroes, tyrants, butchers, scholars, brutal expansionists, explorers, and so much more leading back to the soldiery of the first age. An enormous mantle of responsibility and pressure rests on your shoulders, disrespect it at your own peril.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T03:51:53-07:00","id":906307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=906165#post906165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was it? I thought it was 1/10 per DB parent, with a +1 for a Breeding 4 parent, and +2 for a Breeding 5 parent.<br /> So, two Breeding 5 parents would have a 60% chance per kid, but two Breeding 1 parents would only have a 20% chance.<br /> <br /> I don't actually have the 1st ed DB book, this is going from memory, so I might be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>The (mostly ignored) [2e] breeding rules in Scroll of Erata are way worse, with 60% exaltation rate for two low breeding dragon-bloods, to 100% if both have breeding 5.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Both parents are well bred mortal patricians (yes, patrician is the word they used)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1-2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">One is a Dragon-blooded and the other a poor-bred mortal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1-3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">One is a Dragon-blooded and the other a well-bred parent</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1-4</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Both parents are Dragon-blooded</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1-6</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"> add +1 for Breeding 4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"> add +2 for Breeding 5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"> add +3 for Legendary Breeding</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"></td> </tr> </table></div> And then there's Scroll of Hero's Blood Primacy rules that insist that a Dragon-blood mating with another supernatural being (with lower primacy) results in the child almost certainly exalting as a Dragon-blood.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T04:35:30-07:00","id":906319,"title":"","content":"And there's the <i>other</i> side of what vexes me about these conversations.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's morning, and yet I still find the idea of arguing to elaboration why the Dragon Blooded statistics aren't so bad if one doesn't start with a premise of &quot;the writers are idiots&quot; to be something I can't really bare to expend energy on again.<br /> <br /> Do people remember when Holden linked to Malcolm Sheppard talking about the logistics of the vampire city of Enoch? I would link to it but, you know, copy-paste shenanigans.<br /> <br /> I'll just summarise the point of how it's better to approach these kinds of things as complications that inspire plot points rather than things to snark about on the Internet.<br /> <br /> Although, as one little concession to snarking on the Internet, I'll note with bemusement the assertion that there's something inconsistent in the idea of people who live hedonistically not practicing good birth control, especially when it's available in the form of something as convenient as Maiden Tea. I mean, I suppose sexually active indelibly means irresponsible, eh?<br /> <br /> The assertion that the Dynasty would absolutely be driven to having their children in secret is new, though.<br /> <br /> \u200b{sigh} When am I going to get that backer pdf? I want to have something more positive to focus on.<br /> <br /> I mean, I know what I'm going to get is struggling against all kinds of new complaints and people casting aspersions on writers, but for the interim I can dream.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 06-03-2016, 07:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T05:01:44-07:00","id":906325,"title":"","content":"Honestly I think the 2e parent-based exaltation probabilities actually made a decent amount of sense. If you're building an army of super soldiers that can make more of themselves for you you want them to have a pretty good chance of doing so. I mean, what are you supposed to do with a load of mortal kids in the middle of a war against the Titans? 60% sounds entirely reasonable. Maybe even a bit low.<br /> <br /> It's better if Dragon Blooded can ensure the next generation <i>without </i>fucking like rabbits, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T05:42:48-07:00","id":906339,"title":"","content":"Or possibly, <i>approaching the setting from the perspective of prioritizing the mechanization of specifically the processes of the Titanomachy and not any of the events of the last five thousand years</i> is more the problem.<br /> <br /> Also I contend that considering what a Solar with War, Lore, Medicine, Presence, <i>or</i> Sail can do with a training montage, there's no reason to assume that Dragon-Blooded would deride mortals as useless in a conflict.<br /> <br /> (&quot;But the mortals are just children!&quot;, you say? So are the ones who Exalt as Dragon-Blooded.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T05:47:54-07:00","id":906344,"title":"","content":"Context is important here. I'm talking about one specific mechanic that was decided back then and has had no means or reason to change since. The events of the last five thousand years are <i>completely fucking irrelevant</i> here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T06:38:29-07:00","id":906372,"title":"","content":"Just because the Dragons wanted their chosen to have 100% exaltation rates does not mean they did have 100% exaltation rates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T06:51:59-07:00","id":906380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=906319#post906319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there's the <i>other</i> side of what vexes me about these conversations.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's morning, and yet I still find the idea of arguing to elaboration why the Dragon Blooded statistics aren't so bad if one doesn't start with a premise of &quot;the writers are idiots&quot; to be something I can't really bare to expend energy on again.<br /> <br /> Do people remember when Holden linked to Malcolm Sheppard talking about the logistics of the vampire city of Enoch? I would link to it but, you know, copy-paste shenanigans.<br /> <br /> I'll just summarise the point of how it's better to approach these kinds of things as complications that inspire plot points rather than things to snark about on the Internet.</div> </div> </div> </div>These aren't idle critiques, though; several people (wastevens, maybe? I know I did, at one point) have actually built population models to try to make the book's numbers work. They don't.<br /> <br /> Either the book is wrong when it describes how many children the Dragon-Blooded have; or it is wrong when it describes their Exaltation rate; or it is wrong when it describes their average lifespan. If it's the first, they have birth rates waaaaay below those of modern developed countries, and all this &quot;encouraged to breed&quot; stuff is nonsense; if it's the third, Dragon-Blooded culture should reflect that they're <i>hemorrhaging</i> Exalts, to the tune of &quot;Half of the survivors dead every ten years.&quot; I like the second option.<br /> <br /> I mean, even the writers have said that no one's ever cared about the math of DB population dynamics; I'm fine with starting from the position of assuming competence, but we're pretty far past &quot;starting,&quot; here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T07:49:48-07:00","id":906410,"title":"","content":"Maybe if we can figure out something that works here it might make it into 3e canon. You never know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T08:02:18-07:00","id":906416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=906410#post906410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe if we can figure out something that works here it might make it into 3e canon. You never know.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm pretty sure that using anything we discuss on those boards directly in the books is somewhere between unprofessional and kind of illegal.<br /> <br /> Even if it wasn't, I would not want the books to go into that level of intricacy regardless of what kind of numbers they give for the Dragon Blooded, or anything else, because I can't imagine that looking anything other than clunky.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T08:40:15-07:00","id":906434,"title":"","content":"So they leave the intricacy here and just quote something in the same ball park as our numbers. Problem solved.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Dumb rule anyway...</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T09:14:14-07:00","id":906456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=906416#post906416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure that using anything we discuss on those boards directly in the books is somewhere between unprofessional and kind of illegal.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In rogue trader I've seen complex and a detailed thread on how long it would take for a ship to accelerate and decelerate into a solar system be summed in a later supplement as one sentence, roughly: &quot;A ship can expect to take two to three weeks from jumping near a system to get to a planet of interest in the inner system.&quot; <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=906416#post906416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if it wasn't, I would not want the books to go into that level of intricacy regardless of what kind of numbers they give for the Dragon Blooded, or anything else, because I can't imagine that looking anything other than clunky.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand them not wanting to put literal direct numbers, that can be poked and prodded at and twisted around against them to make no sense. The simple fact is that, typically IRL - populations grow exponentially up to the carry capacity of the land and technology. From my understanding of anthropology - as soon as humans figured out farming and decent medicine, the population boomed ever since - with periodic lulls. DB's with access to charms and the remnants of 1st age technology, and terrestrial circle sorcery, but staying at just 10,000 for centuries on end requires explanations on multiple levels for it to make sense. <br /> <br /> I'm supremely hopeful the current Devs either have better math, or have strong setting reasons for their being only 10,000 DBs in 768. Maybe the number fluctuates a lot more than DBs in the realm would like to admit. In fact - I'm fine with just 10,000 so long as there is some kind of throw away to us math nerds who want the numbers to make sense. To say &quot;no one is interested in DB population dynamics&quot; is a total lie - it's the previous Devs who weren't interested... Given how many rpg players end up in engineering, scientific or programming professions and can setup a simple simulation and point out the problems here... I would like to think that it will be addressed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T09:21:37-07:00","id":906466,"title":"","content":"I don't think the number was <i>ever</i> supposed to be literally 10,000. That's more like a figure of speech for &quot;a lot&quot;. Like how &quot;Myriad&quot; doesn't literally mean 10,000 any more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T09:43:56-07:00","id":906480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=906466#post906466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the number was <i>ever</i> supposed to be literally 10,000. That's more like a figure of speech for &quot;a lot&quot;. Like how &quot;Myriad&quot; doesn't literally mean 10,000 any more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough - the 10,000 could be the &quot;propoganda&quot; number in DB culture in the Realm.<br /> <br /> Anyhow - rereading this thread and my own posts - I think for this game what I'll do is say that DB's reproduction is low and mysterious. I'll keep the Breeding background for power purposes, but chuck out the fertility rules altogether.<br /> <br /> Obviously the DB's population would be designed to grow for the war with the Titanomachy. Much is made of the DB blood over time running &quot;less pure&quot; in the fluff - and perhaps the 2e canon reproduction rates are what it would have been in the first age. Now, in the fallen Second Age - two DB's are very lucky to have a child once per ten years, and even when sexually active can go decades, and even centuries in between children. Such children do Exalt most of the time, but not all. A DB and a mortal have children as normal but it is uncommon, even rare for them to have a child that Exalts. Patricians very rarely exalt, and outside of these lineages, Exalting as a DB is pretty much like winning the lottery - odds are 1 in 10,000,000 births.<br /> <br /> This way my PCs can think strategically about this. Marrying mortal means lots of patrician children. Marrying an Exalt can involve decades of pain - waiting for the DB woman to get pregnant. (Anyone read up on IRL women &amp; couples trying to have children for a long time? It can make people go crazy.) A plot point could be made of trying to figure out forgotten DB eugenics to increase their fertility and involves story telling and problem solving by the players. Maybe they have to make a pilgrimage to the elemental poles and try and contact the sleeping Elemental Dragons. Maybe they have to find a way into Autochthon and wake him in order to repair damaged DB exaltations. Something like that - which I think would be more enjoyable than munckining manses, elementals and harems.<br /> <br /> Also - another factor left out of DB populations is the % that become celibate monks in the Immaculate order. I don't think we're ever given a hard number, but losing a certain % that never reproduce will crimp long term population numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":".  more stuff 06-03-2016, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T10:18:13-07:00","id":906518,"title":"","content":"The closest we ever got to direct numbers on Terrestrial Exalted was back in the First Edition Storyteller Guide, in the Q&amp;A section answered directly by Grabowski (who basically was the original designer for most of Exalted).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Q: How many Exalted are there?<br /> <br /> A: As many as you want there to be. As the game was originally posited, there were more than one hundred and less than two hundred Solar Exalted. There are between three and four hundred Lunars, a hundred or so each of Sidereal and Abyssal Exalted. In contrast to these tiny numbers, there are more than ten thousand Terrestrial Exalted in Creation - in the Realm, there is roughly one Terrestrial Exalt for every five thousand citizens, and this doesn't count Outcastes, Exalted inhabitants of Lookshy or the rural bloodlines of the Northern Threshold nobility. </div> </div> </div>Also, I think people who take the 2nd edition rules for Exalting and applying those to the game as a whole are making a mistake. Those rules were intended to be guidelines to be used for PC's (their children), not to be a broad rule about Dragon Blooded in the entire setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 06-03-2016, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T10:50:55-07:00","id":906548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=906466#post906466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the number was <i>ever</i> supposed to be literally 10,000. That's more like a figure of speech for &quot;a lot&quot;. Like how &quot;Myriad&quot; doesn't literally mean 10,000 any more.</div> </div> </div> </div>What the number is matters a lot less than whether it's stable, though - and the game does seem to assume that, in 2e.<br /> <br /> (Consider how the description of the Realm looks different if they can, today, field vastly more Dragon-Blooded than at any point since their founding.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T11:09:22-07:00","id":906563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=906243#post906243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal headcanon is that DBs have (but may not have had, before the Great Contagion) a low fertility rate amongst themselves, and a VERY low rate with non-DBs. Their children do usually exalt, though - especially if both parents are DBs, and if they have high Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for this, I like it a lot. DB society as described actually makes sense if you just assume DB's are a lot less fecund then baseline humans. As long as you avoid being too scientific about exactly <i>why</i> they are less fertile then it also gives the ST enough latitude to shut down attempts to &quot;gamify&quot; babymaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T11:29:10-07:00","id":906581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=906563#post906563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for this, I like it a lot. DB society as described actually makes sense if you just assume DB's are a lot less fecund then baseline humans. As long as you avoid being too scientific about exactly <i>why</i> they are less fertile then it also gives the ST enough latitude to shut down attempts to &quot;gamify&quot; babymaking.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But since this is an Ex2 thread, we must explain everything!<br /> <br /> As a fail safe against diluting the bloodlines, Dragonblooded aren't all that fertile with non- Dragonblooded. The rare cases of a Dragonblooded breeding with a mortal in the First Age was always scandalous. After the Great Contagion, the population was so low that Dragonblooded had no choice but to have children with mortals. Thus there is enough mortal blooded in the Dragonblooded bloodlines to cause general low fertility. <br /> <br /> /The Ghost of Ex2 Past<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T11:36:12-07:00","id":906588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=906581#post906581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But since this is an Ex2 thread, we must explain everything!<br /> <br /> As a fail safe against diluting the bloodlines, Dragonblooded aren't all that fertile with non- Dragonblooded. The rare cases of a Dragonblooded breeding with a mortal in the First Age was always scandalous. After the Great Contagion, the population was so low that Dragonblooded had no choice but to have children with mortals. Thus there is enough mortal blooded in the Dragonblooded bloodlines to cause general low fertility.<br /> <br /> /The Ghost of Ex2 Past</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like that explanation - DB's never that fertile to begin with, and breeding with mortals, starting at the end of the 1st age - rising in the Shogunate, and becoming commonplace in the dawn of the Scarlet Empire has not just diluted their power (the +motes benefit of Breeding) - but also their fecundity as well to the point now that it is permanently damaged - and then we can go back to my post on what happens in game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T12:19:57-07:00","id":906625,"title":"","content":"Also, for those wondering what the devs will say - I did some more googling on this topic to find old threads - on rpg.net <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?745142-Exalted-Ask-the-Devs-pt2-(Hidden-Meaning-Behind-Veiled-Words-Style)/page59\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php...-Style)/page59</a> , Stephen LS has said that the 2e demographics will be tossed out. There's some more discussion in that part of the thread. Figured i'd share.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T12:45:14-07:00","id":906644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=906563#post906563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for this, I like it a lot. DB society as described actually makes sense if you just assume DB's are a lot less fecund then baseline humans. As long as you avoid being too scientific about exactly <i>why</i> they are less fertile then it also gives the ST enough latitude to shut down attempts to &quot;gamify&quot; babymaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you like it!<br /> <br /> Also, I should note that I specifically call out the higher-Essence parents have better odds of Db offspring (and, I forgot to mention, higher fertility) so that nobody can say &quot;if DBs have a hard time getting kids, the women should be trying full-time.&quot; No, the women should be out having awesome adventures in their youth, so that when they are established, respectable satraps and generals, they'll have better odds of popping an heir. The men, likewise. Adventure!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=906581#post906581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a fail safe against diluting the bloodlines, Dragonblooded aren't all that fertile with non- Dragonblooded. The rare cases of a Dragonblooded breeding with a mortal in the First Age was always scandalous. After the Great Contagion, the population was so low that Dragonblooded had no choice but to have children with mortals. Thus there is enough mortal blooded in the Dragonblooded bloodlines to cause general low fertility.</div> </div> </div> </div>...except in Lookshy, which is why they can be in constant wars of attrition, but bring their numbers back up far more quickly than The Realm.<br /> <br /> This isn't the explanation I would go for (since I don't much like treating aspects of the Exaltation as if they were designed by engineers), but it's pretty clever. I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":2168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","user":"Chejop Kejak","date":". 06-03-2016, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T19:47:16-07:00","id":906907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=906518#post906518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I think people who take the 2nd edition rules for Exalting and applying those to the game as a whole are making a mistake. Those rules were intended to be guidelines to be used for PC's (their children), not to be a broad rule about Dragon Blooded in the entire setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Great point. As a ST I labored under the assumption for years that the rules for PCs applied to everyone.<br /> <br /> That being said, I once ran an enlightened mortal/godblood campaign (that eventually turned Solar) where the PCs were members of House Iselsi though they were distant kin to each other. They stumbled onto a plot by one faction of the House who had immediately after the House's disgrace developed a eugenics program to attempt to mass produce DBs for the House.<br /> <br /> After two or three generations, and applying all the modifiers to increase likelihood for exaltation, they had an exalt success rate of 70%. The 30% who didn't exalt were Terrestrial Half-Castes (before that was officially retconned and for good reason).<br /> <br /> The half-castes were trained to increase their essence to 3. IIRC, when Terrestrial half-castes should reach essence 4, they immediately got to reroll for exaltation. They could only fail on a roll of a 1 which couldn't be mitigated by spending a willpower point.<br /> <br /> The handful that failed to exalt were given positions of prominence over the mortal peasants of which there were many at the main location. By RY 768 they had around 1,000 DBs who were raised from birth to believe that eventually they'd take control of the Realm and thus the future of Creation. <br /> <br /> The plan was to infiltrate and eventually take over the Immaculate Order which they successfully pulled off. Having control of the IO allowed them to wield incredible social power. They used that power to make things easier for Iselsi.<br /> <br /> Many of the DBs who had not trained in the IO martial arts infiltrated House Tepet after its devastating loss to the Bull thrusting the House back into a position of power. The elders of the House realized too late that these &quot;lost eggs&quot; were actually all in cahoots and had their own agenda. That agenda allowed House Iselsi to operate a little more openly.<br /> <br /> Some may wonder how a disgraced House was able to pull it off. The DBs in that faction weren't alone. A few members of House Iselsi had become Celestial Exalted since the House fell. With a handful of Solars, a few older Lunars and a gold faction Sidereal to muddy the waters of Iselsi's destiny, they were able to greatly enhance Iselsi's power and influence throughout the Realm and Creation. Eventually their disgraced status was revoked by the Realm's Deliberative, and the House was restored to good standing. Although they never managed to position themselves to take over the Realm, they did manage to save the House.<br /> <br /> TL;DR: 2E DB breeding and terrestrial half-caste rules allowed for game/setting breaking changes to be made in a relatively short amount of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T21:03:58-07:00","id":906935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=906907#post906907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This. Great point. As a ST I labored under the assumption for years that the rules for PCs applied to everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div> The thing to remember is that this is a story. Ordinary things will happen to the background cast; extraordinary things happen to the main characters. That's <i>why</i> they're the main characters. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=906907#post906907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> TL;DR: 2E DB breeding and terrestrial half-caste rules allowed for game/setting breaking changes to be made in a relatively short amount of time.</div> </div> </div> </div> Wait. There were <i>rules</i> for them? I only found a brief textual mention of terrestrial half-bloods in CoCD:Blessed Isles.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T21:44:39-07:00","id":906957,"title":"","content":"We got rules for Terrestrial half-castes in 1st edition and a mention of them in early 2nd edition. However, it was decided after Blessed Isle was released that Terrestrial half-castes didn't belong, so when we later got the book detailing half-castes, the Terrestrial version was not included.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T22:52:17-07:00","id":906982,"title":"","content":"To be fair, Celestial Half-Castes also introduce some key problems with the role of DBs in the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T23:41:36-07:00","id":907003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=906982#post906982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, Celestial Half-Castes also introduce some key problems with the role of DBs in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Terrestrial half-castes though heavily change the structure of the Realm and of other Dragon Blooded communities (such as Lookshy) by blurring the boundary between mortal and Dragon Blooded. They're a sort of &quot;half&quot; Terrestrial that received a partial blessing from the Dragons or something, and by the rules there would have been tens of thousands, or more, half-castes running around the Realm. That would have a <i>huge</i> impact.<br /> <br /> Celestial half-castes were also bad, for different reasons as you mentioned, such as the issue with &quot;mass produced&quot; humans running around with Celestial and Solar Charms (a problem that Akuma had as well) which, unfortunately, made them a lot better and more useful than Dragon Blooded on account of the inherent suckiness of the DB charmset in 2nd edition compared to that of Celestial Exalted. <br /> <br /> But really, don't get me started on half-castes. Dumb, dumb, dumb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T00:28:40-07:00","id":907013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=907003#post907003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But really, don't get me started on half-castes. Dumb, dumb, dumb.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was my point, yeah.<br /> <br /> I have no advice on how to reconcile Half-Castes with the setting, because my answer will always be &quot;ignore it <i>so hard</i>.&quot; I can see the case for Terrestrial ones being the worst, just as I can see the case for the worst hangings being ones where your neck doesn't snap. Which is to say - I'm so avidly avoiding both, it's academic, however logical the premise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T01:28:50-07:00","id":907029,"title":"","content":"A simple solution to all of these might just be to say that children born later in the birth-order are less likely to Exalt; that is, your firstborn is very likely to Exalt, whereas your sixth child is significantly less likely to. This has a degree of basis in both mythology and real-world culture, so it's very relatable.<br /> <br /> (Seventh children might have a spike in their chance of Exaltation because mythology.)<br /> <br /> If you want to worry about such things, you could also say that for those with a non-Terrestrial parent, having a Terrestrial mother helps more than having a Terrestrial father (although the decrease in chance of Exaltation as you have more children would affect both men and women.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 06-04-2016, 04:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T01:45:28-07:00","id":907033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=907029#post907029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A simple solution to all of these might just be to say that children born later in the birth-order are less likely to Exalt; that is, your firstborn is very likely to Exalt, whereas your sixth child is significantly less likely to. This has a degree of basis in both mythology and real-world culture, so it's very relatable.<br /> <br /> (Seventh children might have a spike in their chance of Exaltation because mythology.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this because it allows for both a majority of mortal dynasts and (firstborn) dynasts who are a terrible disappointment for not Exalting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T01:58:37-07:00","id":907035,"title":"","content":"I always liked to think that there was a metaphysical component to the Terrestrial Exaltation. By which I mean that maybe when the Host is weakened it is more likely that the exaltation will shine even in diluted lines. That would explain how they are able to bounce back from doomsday events even with dilution and then become less able to exalt, maybe they are rare NOW because the host has as many as twenty to thirty thousand souls (their unity is irrevelant) and it skyrockets when their numbers drop below the original ten thousand. Just a theory, but I have always loved the 'cut one down and another will take their place' part of the DB concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 06-04-2016, 05:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T09:53:44-07:00","id":907144,"title":"","content":"I'm reading some quite interesting things about the dynamics of groups that engage in feuds. Such as the Yanomami people (a group consisting of about 35,000), an ethnic group consisting on many tribes and villages who are given to various states of violence and warfare amongst one another; somewhere between one-third and <i>one-half</i> of their men apparently die in that violence.<br /> <br /> \u200bOf course, the Scarlet Dynasty has limits imposed on how openly it can engage in violence against one another. On the other hand, Exalted probably go charging off into dangerous situations for recreational purposes a lot more often than real life feuding aristocrats and warring tribal groups might do, so it could just about balance out.<br /> <br /> The thing I've always found curious about comparisons to the plague is that they sound like something that assumes a kind of passivity behind why only one third of the Terrestrial Exalted of the Realm make it to old age.<br /> <br /> Actually, that's not true; only one third make it to <i>retirement</i>, with a caveat noting that a sizable number of Dragon Blooded make fortunes that allow them to retire young. So even less than a third make it through their disproportionate proclivity for adventures, military careers, and various levels of interpersonal feuds. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T09:58:07-07:00","id":907149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=907144#post907144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing I've always found curious about comparisons to the plague is that they sound like something that assumes a kind of passivity behind why only one third of the Terrestrial Exalted of the Realm make it to old age.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's reading in something rather entirely beside the point - the point being that being that, to get death rates that high, you have to look at some of the most appalling and culture-warping periods in the last thousand years or so. For a largely-western audience, the Black Death is an easy reference point, even though it <i>still</i> undersells the number (it requires compressing all the plague deaths over decades into ~7 years).<br /> <br /> &quot;Passivity&quot; is irrelevant, but comparable death rates due to active intervention that would be common reference points are, well, harder to come up with - checking some old notes, you need mortality in the range of 7.5% per year, even if you cut the book values substantially. &quot;Russia in WW2&quot; was a horrific, appalling place to be, but it's still a lot safer than that. &quot;A third of our men die to violence&quot; is <i>still a lot lower than 7.5% per annum,</i> and 7.5% is already low for the situation the book presents - the probability table aside, <i>someone</i> writing the DB book thought there were hundreds of new Exalts a year, and, uh, that's nuts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually, that's not true; only one third make it to <i>retirement</i>, with a caveat noting that a sizable number of Dragon Blooded make fortunes that allow them to retire young. So even less than a third make it through their disproportionate proclivity for adventures, military careers, and various levels of interpersonal feuds. </div> </div> </div>The plague-like death rates are entirely incompatible with &quot;a third of them make it to retirement.&quot; They suggest that something like a third of Dragon-Blooded make it to <i>age thirty</i>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=216112#post216112\">We have had this conversation before.</a> The book's numbers cannot be made to work.<br /> <br /> (Edit: One set of numbers that does work: really high Breeding - say, V'neef, and probably just V'neef - gives you 80%+ exaltation rates. Other DB/DB pairings get ~1-10% exaltation rates. Everybody else has a one-in-a-million shot or less - maybe one-in-a-thousand, if one of the partners is a DB. Something around 30 Dragon-Blooded are born or adopted into the Realm every year; something around 30 Realm Dragon-Blooded die every year.<br /> <br /> (In addition to fixing the population dynamics, this has the nice side effect that it removes all incentive to go down What About A Mass Breeding Program Highway, because your thousand-person harem is going to give you maybe one Exalted kid a year, and you won't know who he or she is until you've raised all thousand kids for fifteen years.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 06-04-2016, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T10:18:56-07:00","id":907156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=907029#post907029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A simple solution to all of these might just be to say that children born later in the birth-order are less likely to Exalt; that is, your firstborn is very likely to Exalt, whereas your sixth child is significantly less likely to. This has a degree of basis in both mythology and real-world culture, so it's very relatable.<br /> <br /> (Seventh children might have a spike in their chance of Exaltation because mythology.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's also a good way of doing things! (Though surely in Creation, the spike is at five?)<br /> <br /> Opposite to crumplepunch, I don't want the hordes of unExalted Dynasts this model suggests - really churn 'em out, since you've gotta reach 7/5 anyway, Exalted mothers have no appreciable chance of death by childbirth, and each child has SOME chance of Exaltation. In other words, I <i>love</i> the firstborn in this model, less so their (many) siblings.<br /> <br /> ...which sounds harsh, I think, but isn't meant to be. There's no reason why other people should want the same things from a setting hack that I do. I was breaking down what I see as the implications of this, as a thought exercise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=907035#post907035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always liked to think that there was a metaphysical component to the Terrestrial Exaltation. By which I mean that maybe when the Host is weakened it is more likely that the exaltation will shine even in diluted lines. That would explain how they are able to bounce back from doomsday events even with dilution and then become less able to exalt, maybe they are rare NOW because the host has as many as twenty to thirty thousand souls (their unity is irrevelant) and it skyrockets when their numbers drop below the original ten thousand. Just a theory, but I have always loved the 'cut one down and another will take their place' part of the DB concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Likewise, the big change here is that you are, in effect, declaring that the idea of millions of Terrestrials during the First Age and hundreds of thousands during the Shogunate is unlikely to the point of being impossible. Maybe it's just not something the Dragon-Blooded harken back to in your setting, or maybe that's a myth... but it's not a fact.<br /> <br /> I... might like that, actually. There's tons of ways for the Age of Sorrows to be a fallen era without the roadmap for restoring Creation including &quot;mass-produce Dragon-Blooded&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T10:20:27-07:00","id":907159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=907144#post907144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reading some quite interesting things about the dynamics of groups that engage in feuds. Such as the Yanomami people (a group consisting of about 35,000), an ethnic group consisting on many tribes and villages who are given to various states of violence and warfare amongst one another; somewhere between one-third and <i>one-half</i> of their men apparently die in that violence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though IIRC that characterisation of the Yanomami is fairly controversial amongst anthropologists. (As in, there are huge and bitter fights over it, still ongoing. I'm not going to rule over who is correct, not being an anthropologist.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","name":"Iozz-Sothoth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T10:42:50-07:00","id":907174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/906006-2e-on-the-numbers-of-dragon-blooded?p=907156#post907156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Likewise, the big change here is that you are, in effect, declaring that the idea of millions of Terrestrials during the First Age and hundreds of thousands during the Shogunate is unlikely to the point of being impossible. Maybe it's just not something the Dragon-Blooded harken back to in your setting, or maybe that's a myth... but it's not a fact.<br /> <br /> I... might like that, actually. There's tons of ways for the Age of Sorrows to be a fallen era without the roadmap for restoring Creation including &quot;mass-produce Dragon-Blooded&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> While millions would be out of the question, you could consider that even the Shogunate probably had better medicine and life-extending magic than the current mess. This would mean that you would have a small number of children exalting but many more lasting far longer which would result in a higher number overall, also I image violent DB deaths were rare in the First Age unless they caught their Solar boss on a bad day. The scheme I was thinking was more like a normal 10 percent exaltation chance with 2ed's ludicrous chance when the host is under-strength.<br /> <br /> Although my reasoning is the power that created them wanted an army of self-replicating super-soldiers. You want to make up for severe losses quickly but growing too quickly would mean a decline in quality of training and your ability to arm then properly. <br /> <br /> Like the Incarnas the Dragons probably made something far greater than what they were shooting for. I would use that breeding scheme as a symptom of the never expecting the DBs to grow to such great numbers anymore than the other Incarna intended to create Elder Celestials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 06-04-2016, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}